reeter speak\n50\t      differently.\n51\t  - term: command\n52\t    means: >-\n53\t      One command line a user types to run the greeter, its arguments\n54\t      included. Everything a user sees of the greeter follows from one.\n55\t  - term: exit code\n56\t    means: >-\n57\t      The number the command ends with: 0 when it succeeded, anything\n58\t      else when it did not. Scripts calling the greeter branch on it.\n59\t  - term: standard output\n60\t    means: >-\n61\t      The lines the command prints for its user, its answer and its log\n62\t      records alike. It is the greeter's only visible output.\n63\t\n64\tconcepts:\n65\t  given:\n66\t    - concept: configured greeting\n67\t      means: >-\n68\t        The project's config file sets the greeting to a stated text\n69\t        before the command runs.\n70\t      terms: [greeting, command]\n71\t  when:\n72\t    - concept: a role runs a command\n73\t      means: >-\n74\t        A role runs one stated command line once, in the project\n75\t        directory, and waits for it to exit.\n76\t      terms: [command]\n77\t  then:\n78\t    - concept: exit code\n79\t      means: >-\n80\t        The command the role ran ended with a stated exit code; 0 means\n81\t        it succeeded.\n82\t      terms: [command, exit code]\n83\t    - concept: standard output\n84\t      means: >-\n85\t        A line the command printed on its standard output has a match for\n86\t        a stated pattern, a regular expression.\n87\t      terms: [command, standard output]\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c77b6504-ca78-4e61-ad4d-ac6b19c36bd2","uuid":"c2c3cdc2-6176-431a-84f6-581e7b0cc3b6","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:35:58.209Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"{{CWD}}/tmp/{{RUN_DIR}}/product.yaml","content":"# Product document for the greeter, the host project of the scen-check\n# fixtures that walk the shipped checklist.\n#\n# Its concepts cover every step of the claimed Scenario, and its\n# glossar